hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"996","Bundar told us, Yahya told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, Sa’id al-Maqbari told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Sa’id al-Khudri. On the authority of his father, he said: We were imprisoned on the Day of the Trench until it was just after sunset, and that was before he went down to fight, so when we had enough Fighting, and that is the saying of God Almighty: “And God is sufficient for the believers from fighting, and God is Strong and Mighty.” Surat Al-Ahzab, verse 25. “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded He greeted Bilal, so he performed the noon prayer, meaning the noon prayer, and prayed it as he used to pray it at its time, then he performed the afternoon prayer, as he used to pray it at its time, then He stood for Maghrib and prayed it as he used to pray it at its time.” Bundar narrated it once, saying: Yahya narrated to us, and Othman, meaning Ibn Umar, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, So he mentioned the hadith, and it contained words that were not in his narration when he isolated the hadith from Yahya."
